      "id": "0mjgavr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Sound"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Sound is a form of energy produced by vibrating objects and travels as a mechanical longitudinal wave.",
        "Sound requires a material medium (solid, liquid, or gas) to propagate and cannot travel through a vacuum.",
        "Characteristics of sound waves include amplitude (loudness), frequency (pitch), and wave speed.",
        "An echo occurs due to the reflection of sound when the reflecting surface is at least 17.2 meters away.",
        "Ultrasound refers to sound frequencies above 20,000 Hz and is used in medical imaging, SONAR, and industrial cleaning."
      ],
      "id": "ya9vdyc"
    },
