    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Sound travels fastest in solids, slower in liquids, and slowest in gases; it cannot travel in a vacuum.",
        "Loudness of sound depends on the square of its amplitude, whereas pitch depends on frequency.",
        "To hear a distinct echo, the time gap between the original sound and reflected sound must be at least 0.1 seconds.",
        "SONAR (Sound Navigation and Ranging) utilizes ultrasonic waves to measure underwater distances and depths."
      ],
      "id": "sl89wa4"
